<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21091" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hydrăgōgus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδραγωγός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>that carries off water.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: utendum aquiducis medicamentis, quae
			Graeci hydragoga vocaverunt, Cael. Aur.  Tard. 3, 8,
			119.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hydrage-gos</span></b> , i, f., <i>a plant</i>, <i>called also</i>
			chamaedaphne <i>and</i> daphnites,
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 27</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
